alth how's your  mental health sleeping well what about  your relationships what do you spend  your time doing every day you happy  spending your time doing those things  every day and I was able to carry on  this journal into my digital social  media detox so I was able to see what  the changes were from that transition of  having a life way you check social media  and having a life where you don't check  social media I think the changes are so  subtle that we sometimes don't realize  you know if little things for me like my  memory improved because I was able to  actually pay attention to things that  were happening in the real world more so  than when I was subconsciously always  thinking about my social media accounts  and I think these accounts have a hold  on us in a way that we kind of don't  even realize so keeping a journal can be  a really beneficial way to do this I did  keep my paper journal and then recycled  it or you can keep an electronic journal  type on your laptop whatever but it's  these philosophies that when you look  back after the 30 days can really help  you make a decision as to whether your  social media usage is giving you more  positives or negatives and you know that  can be the catalyst for making you  decide that you want to delete your  social media accounts permanently which  is the decision I made after the 30 days  I just had far too many positives happen  in those 30 days and things that  improved in my life that it kind of  wasn't worth it so it's it's looking  back oh that journal and seeing if it's  worth sacrificing all those things for  so good luck if you do decide to have a  social media detox and if you do decide  that the cons are bigger than the pros  afterwards and you decide to come off  social media forever then well done and  enjoy life in the real world without  incessant and relentless checking of  your phone it is a wonderful place to be  my minimalist just wanted to share a  great minimalist way to enjoy books I  know in my city of Toronto you're able  to get a library card and then you're  able to sign in online  and get ebooks and audiobooks for free  straight to your phone you don't go to  the library at all that's a great way to  enjoy books you can have them on your  phone and read them anywhere or listen  to an audiobook on your commute and it's  a great way to enjoy books and not have  to stop them  hey Ryan and Josh this is Lauren and  Colorado I am responding to Sabrina who  called in on the intentionality or  intentions episode and was asking how  she can continue to remind herself as  her intentions day to day once she has  set them and I've read an article once I  think I found it on LinkedIn that  recommended that you can set your  password to email or to your computer or  to your phone to somehow encompass your  goals so when I decided to go vegan the  word vegan was a part of my password you  know when I had certain goals to reduce  my environmental footprint I use certain  words to remind myself every day that I  typed in my password that I was going to  minimize waste or reduce waste and so it  was actually a really great tip and I've  used it for the past few years and found  it to be really successful  alright y'all that's it for this episode  if you have a question for the  minimalists give us a call for 0 6 2 1 9  7 8 3 9 remember we're all we're  especially looking for questions about  sex and sleep and jobs and business and  I think there was one other Ryan love  the topic of love and so if you have any  questions that are loosely related when  you call up just say hey my question is  about love or whatever and we'll make  sure that your question makes it to the  top of the list or you can call us with  a question about anything else as well  and or you could just know instead of  calling in you send a voicemail right  from your phone the podcast at the  minimalists dot-com and if you leave  here with just one message we hope it's  this love people and use things because  the opposite never works thanks for  listening y'all we'll see you next time  bye and minimus  [Laughter]

